🚨 𝗣𝗨𝗟𝗦𝗘 𝗣𝗔𝗣𝗘𝗥𝗕𝗢𝗬 — 𝗗𝗜𝗚𝗘𝗦𝗧 📰
October 24, 2026 · 14:00 ET

🔒 @LibertySwapFi urges ZKX Wallet users to update and resync private balances

🛢️ @coinbureau reports US-Iran tensions escalating toward midterms

⚠️ Day 11: @_pulseheartwin_ says no official update on Richard Heart's Istanbul detention

Full article & crypto details below:

❤️ THE RICHARD HEART CASE

No official confirmation of Richard Heart's legal status emerged in this window; community monitoring continues alongside unverified speculation. Treat all timeline and legal-strategy claims below as community commentary, not confirmed fact.

@_pulseheartwin_ stated flatly "Richard is on day 11 in Istanbul and still no update," reiterating that the situation remains in limbo with no court decision or official statement confirmed by authorities.

The same account pushed back on fraud/securities narratives by invoking the 2023-2025 SEC case, writing "February 2025: the SEC case was dismissed. No fine. No settlement. No admission. Headlines are not verdicts" — relevant historical context, though not evidence regarding the current detention matter.

@_pulseheartwin_ also floated a defense-style argument about transparency, noting Heart "told everyone on camera what he owns. watches, cars, all of it... and that's basically what they found on him," framing it rhetorically as inconsistent with a concealment narrative — explicitly speculative, not a legal finding.

In a lighter community exchange, @dr_pegger reinforced a "silence is discipline, not weakness" framing, writing that "multi-jurisdiction cases punish loose talk" and that "nothing said in Istanbul can be allowed to hurt RH in Helsinki or at Interpol" — an unconfirmed strategic read from a community account, not legal counsel.

No bridge-related or newly filed court documents were reported by monitored accounts in this window.

👥 THE PULSE CROWD

Community mood this afternoon mixed resilience-themed posts about PulseChain's uptime with a notable privacy-infrastructure update from LibertySwap, plus scattered HEX price banter and lighthearted chatter.

@LibertySwapFi issued a direct operational notice: "Make sure you're using ZKX Wallet v0.0.55 or v0.0.56," followed by a detailed call to action urging users to "open your ZKX Wallet or Railway Wallet and sync all pending PPOIs," noting four pending POIs with unidentified owners and reminding holders "It is YOUR MONEY" — a concrete privacy-wallet maintenance update tied to the ZKX/Railgun-style private balance system.

@_pulseheartwin_ marked a PulseChain milestone, writing "PulseChain mainnet: May 2023. Since then, a block every 10 seconds. Through bear markets, FUD, lawsuits and headlines. It doesn't care what you think of it. It just keeps working" — an uptime/resilience narrative from the community, not independently verified network statistics.

@29KingsMan96 offered bullish enthusiasm toward LibertySwap's momentum ("Bullishhhhhhhhhhhhhh 🚀🚀🚀") and separately claimed "Billions will flow into PulseChain during PulseChain Privacy Season!!!" — an unverified, speculative prediction with no supporting data.

@LibertySwapFi, responding to community debate about decentralization, argued PulseChain is "more decentralized than Ethereum" because it doesn't require "Vitalik or institutions," and claimed its security model is stronger "after numerous hard forks without fundamental improvements" to Ethereum's — a self-interested project claim, not an independent audit finding.

@yourfriendSOMMI posted on a separate asset, $XBT, saying "Good to see they are selling it down for us to buy more," setting a speculative "Ultimate Target... like $3000-$10,000 if BTC can reach $200K" — explicitly framed as personal speculation, figures unconfirmed.

@_pulseheartwin_ added light market color on HEX, joking "hexicans looking at -2% like it's a typo" and "grass is the only green thing in my portfolio today," reflecting a soft-red day in sentiment rather than confirmed price data.

@CrusherHODL kept engagement upbeat with brief exclamatory support ("YES WE ARE!") in ongoing community banter, while @dr_pegger scattered short replies of solidarity across threads, including "Diamond hands unite!"

👥 Today's Pulse Crowd Voices: @LibertySwapFi, @_pulseheartwin_, @29KingsMan96, @yourfriendSOMMI, @CrusherHODL, @dr_pegger, @zkxwallet, @Hexangelo5

🔗 ON CHAIN

No significant bridge inflow/outflow figures for PulseChain were reported by monitored accounts in this window. No whale transfers, TVL shifts, or notable DEX volume spikes tied to PLS or HEX surfaced in the collected data. The one concrete on-chain-adjacent development was @LibertySwapFi's ZKX Wallet v0.0.55/v0.0.56 update prompting users to resync pending PPOIs (private balance syncs), with four pending POIs of unidentified ownership still outstanding — an operational/privacy-infrastructure item rather than a volume or flow metric. Broader chain activity metrics remained unreported this cycle.

🌎 THE BIGGER PICTURE

Macro attention centered heavily on escalating US-Iran tensions and their knock-on effects for commodities and risk assets heading into a volatile week. According to @coinbureau, US officials say Trump is "leaning toward a return to major combat" with Iran, citing a restocking USS George Washington, an inbound carrier strike group, embassy staff pullbacks across 13 countries, and Brent crude climbing to roughly $117 — its highest since April — though the outlet notes "no final decision has been made," with any strikes reportedly being prepared for after the midterm elections.

@cryptorover warned that "the next week could be very dangerous for global markets," flagging a stacked calendar: US markets reopening Monday amid Iran strike warnings, employment and housing data Tuesday, an FOMC decision and Kevin Warsh press conference Wednesday, PCE inflation and GDP data Thursday (inflation estimated at 3.6%, up from 3.4%), and Japan/wage data Friday — concluding that hot inflation plus hawkish Fed signals "could" trigger a selloff across stocks, metals, and crypto; this is a forward-looking scenario, not a guaranteed outcome.

@Cointelegraph reported that over a third of all ETH supply — roughly 36% — is now staked, an on-chain record suggesting holders are "locking up" rather than selling, per the outlet's framing.

@zerohedge flagged a reported Houthi missile attack on Saudi territory, including the East-West pipeline, adding another geopolitical variable to oil-market risk this week.

⚡ PAPERBOY RADAR

❤️ Heartbeat: Not applicable this window — no new @RichardHeartWin posts detected.

👥 Pulse Crowd: LibertySwap pushes ZKX Wallet update; community mixes resilience posts with light HEX banter.

🔗 On-Chain: No major bridge/TVL/whale data reported; ZKX wallet sync was the lone operational item.

🌎 Bigger Picture: Iran tensions push Brent toward $117 as traders brace for a heavy Fed/data week.

🗞️ THE LAST DROP

Today's signal was geopolitical, not on-chain. Oil climbing toward $117 on Iran-strike fears, paired with a loaded Fed/inflation calendar next week, is the macro backdrop every trader should be watching — @cryptorover's "dangerous week" framing deserves attention even if outcomes stay unconfirmed. On the PulseChain side, the real news wasn't price chatter but infrastructure: @LibertySwapFi's ZKX Wallet update and PPOI resync call matters more long-term than any single day's HEX dip. The Richard Heart situation remains stuck in a familiar holding pattern — day 11 with no official word, per @_pulseheartwin_, and community speculation filling the information vacuum on both sides. Nothing here confirms a legal outcome. Watch Monday's market reopen and the FOMC decision midweek; those will likely matter more than any single tweet.

Which story are you tracking closer this weekend — the Iran-driven macro risk or the ZKX privacy rollout?

